meta {
  name: Clone Site Admin Template
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/radiology-tests/{{siteAdminRadiologyTestId}}/clone
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "masterDataId": "{{masterDataId}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.id) bru.setEnvVar("clonedRadiologyTestId", data.id);
}

docs {
  Clone a SITE_ADMIN radiology-test template (the `:id` in the URL) into the
  caller's tenant catalogue. Business JWT. **Only `masterDataId` is sent in the
  body** — `tenantId`/`branchId` come from the JWT and the target master data,
  never the client (CLAUDE.md §4.7). Captures `clonedRadiologyTestId`.

  Behaviour: deep-copies the flat template with a fresh UUID, sets
  `source = "TENANT"`, `tenantId` (JWT), `branchId` (from the master data),
  `masterDataId` (body), `clonedFromId = template.id`, and seeds a fresh
  `versionHistory` v1.

  - `siteAdminRadiologyTestId` is a live SITE_ADMIN template → else 404
    `RADIOLOGY_TEST_NOT_FOUND`.
  - `masterDataId` must belong to the caller's tenant → else 404
    `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND`.
  - 409 `RADIOLOGY_TEST_NAME_CONFLICT` / `RADIOLOGY_TEST_CODE_CONFLICT` if the
    template's name/code already exists (active) in the target master data.
}
